#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:58
#: 7da5ca907c9748849c60a476b5c2b43a
msgid "These GPS can incorporate real time kinematic data, either internally generated or externally provided, to improve the precision of the position estimate from the normal GPS meter range down to the centimeter range (see :ref:`common-rtk-correction`). This increased precision also allows for \"Moving Baseline\" yaw estimates using two devices on a vehicle with certain RTK GPSes (F9P based) or dedicated Moving Baseline GPSes. See :ref:`common-gps-for-yaw`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:109
#: feaffc09b5d249faac6cd1cf1a4b1692
msgid "a version of firmware for the CubePilot HERE 4 DroneCAN RTK GPS is available `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/AP_Periph/latest/Here4AP/>`__ that includes evolving ArduPilot improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:111
#: dc6caffaac8a466aa930fc14d57fc830
msgid "It is important that a GPS be connected to the first SERIALx port that has its ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` parameter set to \"5\" (GPS) since it will stop searching for GPS during boot-up if not found on the first port configured for GPS protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:115
#: a24c743a075545a6b32266d42bba0993
msgid "Moving Baseline (GPS for Yaw) Capable"
